          "heading": "Owen Doyle condemns Michael Hooper and Sir Steve Hansen regarding Piardi",
          "body": "Former IRFU director of referees Owen Doyle has labelled recent comments from Michael Hooper and Sir Steve Hansen as “totally out of order.” The pair had suggested that World Rugby should prevent Italian official Andrea Piardi from refereeing future Australia matches, citing concerns over player and referee welfare. Doyle challenged this stance, arguing that the criticism levelled at Piardi following the Wallabies' win over the Springboks was misdirected, particularly as the referee contended with significant technical failures regarding TMO communications."
