          "body": "The high-profile legal action regarding brain injuries in rugby remains in a precarious position as claimants continue to face a significant £2.8m legal bill. While recent court battles have prevented the cases from being thrown out, the financial burden remains the primary obstacle to the proceedings continuing. With the deadline to settle these mounting legal fees approaching this month, the future of the litigation against governing bodies remains uncertain for all parties involved, including those within the Scottish game."
